theory:
## Common invariant Patterns

### Pattern 1: Range-Bound Numbers
```xiom
pub type Percentage = Int
  invariant: this >= 0;
  invariant: this <= 100;

pub type NonNegative = Int
  invariant: this >= 0;

pub type Speed = Float64
  invariant: this >= 0.0;
  invariant: this <= 299792458.0;  // Speed of light
```

### Pattern 2: Non-Empty
```xiom
pub type NonEmptyVec[T] = Vec[T]
  invariant: this.len() > 0;

pub type NonBlankStr = Str
  invariant: this.len() > 0;
  invariant: this.trim().len() > 0;  // Not just whitespace
```

### Pattern 3: Validated Strings
```xiom
pub type Username = Str
  invariant: this.len() >= 3;
  invariant: this.len() <= 20;
  invariant: this.chars().all(|c| c.is_alphanumeric());

pub type HexColor = Str
  invariant: this.len() == 7;
  invariant: this.starts_with("#");
```

### Pattern 4: Cross-Field Validation
```xiom
pub type TimeRange = {
  start: Int;
  end: Int;
} invariant: this.start >= 0;
  invariant: this.end <= 86400;
  invariant: this.start <= this.end;
```

### Pattern 5: Enum Validity
```xiom
pub type HttpResponse = {
  status: Int;
  body: Str;
} invariant: this.status >= 100;
  invariant: this.status < 600;
  invariant: this.status != 204 || this.body.len() == 0;
```

